---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security & Privacy"
  description="Security and privacy posture for Alif Rafi Tulusena's personal portfolio."
>

  <section class="site-container">
    <div
      class="editorial-grid pb-20 pt-16 md:pb-32 md:pt-24"
    >
      <div>
        <p class="mono-label text-muted">
          Security / 2026
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="editorial-content">
        <h1
          class="max-w-[1100px] text-[clamp(3.6rem,7.2vw,8rem)] leading-[0.91] font-medium tracking-[-0.065em]"
        >
          Small attack surface.
          <span class="text-muted">
            Explicit boundaries.
          </span>
        </h1>

        <p
          class="mt-10 max-w-[980px] text-[clamp(1.05rem,1.35vw,1.3rem)] leading-[1.7] text-muted"
        >
          This portfolio is intentionally implemented as a static site with
          minimal runtime behavior and no server-side collection of visitor data.
          This page documents the security decisions and limitations behind it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="site-container py-20 md:py-28">
    <div
      class="editorial-grid border-t border-line pt-8"
      data-reveal
    >
      <div>
        <p class="mono-label text-muted">
          01 / Architecture
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="editorial-content">
        <h2 class="section-title">
          Static by design.
        </h2>

        <div class="case-copy mt-10">
          <p>
            The deployed portfolio is generated by Astro and published as static
            HTML, CSS, images, fonts, and a small amount of same-origin JavaScript.
            There is no application server, database, authentication layer,
            session storage, or server-side contact endpoint.
          </p>

          <p>
            Contact is handled through a <code>mailto:</code> link. The portfolio
            itself therefore does not receive, process, or retain message content.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="site-container py-20 md:py-28">
    <div
      class="editorial-grid border-t border-line pt-8"
      data-reveal
    >
      <div>
        <p class="mono-label text-muted">
          02 / Browser Controls
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="editorial-content">
        <h2 class="section-title">
          Restrict what the page is allowed to load.
        </h2>

        <div class="case-copy mt-10">
          <p>
            A document-level Content Security Policy limits scripts, network
            connections, media, fonts, images, frames, and other runtime resources
            to the portfolio's own origin wherever practical.
          </p>

          <p>
            Inline scripts are not allowed. Inline styles remain permitted because
            some current visual components use inline style declarations; this is
            a known trade-off rather than an accidental exception.
          </p>

          <p>
            An explicit referrer policy limits the amount of URL information sent
            when visitors follow cross-origin links.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="site-container py-20 md:py-28">
    <div
      class="editorial-grid border-t border-line pt-8"
      data-reveal
    >
      <div>
        <p class="mono-label text-muted">
          03 / Data & Privacy
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="editorial-content">
        <h2 class="section-title">
          Publish only what belongs in public.
        </h2>

        <div class="case-copy mt-10">
          <p>
            The site does not intentionally use cookies, analytics, advertising
            trackers, or behavioral profiling.
          </p>

          <p>
            Some portfolio material originates from real institutional systems.
            Before publication, sensitive values are reviewed and redacted. The
            public portfolio is not intended to expose credentials, private student
            identifiers, private contact details, or non-public application data.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="site-container py-20 md:py-28">
    <div
      class="editorial-grid border-t border-line pt-8"
      data-reveal
    >
      <div>
        <p class="mono-label text-muted">
          04 / Supply Chain
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="editorial-content">
        <h2 class="section-title">
          Treat the build pipeline as part of the product.
        </h2>

        <div class="case-copy mt-10">
          <p>
            Production installs use the committed npm lockfile through
            <code>npm ci</code>. Dependency checks run on a schedule, and
            Dependabot is configured for both npm packages and GitHub Actions.
          </p>

          <p>
            Deployment actions are pinned to immutable full commit SHAs and jobs
            receive only the GitHub token permissions they need. The build job is
            read-only; deployment receives Pages and OIDC permissions only in the
            dedicated deployment job.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="site-container py-20 md:py-28">
    <div
      class="editorial-grid border-t border-line pt-8"
      data-reveal
    >
      <div>
        <p class="mono-label text-muted">
          05 / Boundaries
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="editorial-content">
        <h2 class="section-title">
          External systems are not part of this security scope.
        </h2>

        <div class="case-copy mt-10">
          <p>
            Project pages may link to GitHub, LinkedIn, institutional sites, or
            staging environments. Those destinations are controlled by their own
            operators and are outside this portfolio's vulnerability-testing scope.
          </p>

          <p>
            Security research against a third-party system should only happen with
            that owner's explicit authorization.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="site-container py-20 md:py-28">
    <div
      class="editorial-grid border-y border-line py-10"
      data-reveal
    >
      <div>
        <p class="mono-label text-muted">
          Report
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="editorial-content">
        <p class="editorial-copy text-muted">
          If you identify an issue in this portfolio or repository, please report
          it to
          <a
            href={`mailto:${site.email}`}
            class="ml-1 underline underline-offset-4"
          >
            {site.email}
          </a>.
          The repository also contains a public
          <a
            href="https://github.com/AlsenaRT/AlsenaRT.github.io/security/policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="ml-1 underline underline-offset-4"
          >
            vulnerability disclosure policy ↗
          </a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
